From 89a1fa191535cb2dd5808ae025e21ba6e62ad81e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c6-agent <agent@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:13:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/10] c6: every variable definition must be initialized

VLA is the only exception (C forbids initializing a variable length array).
'extern' declarations, parameters, struct/union members, typedefs and alias
objects are declarations, not definitions, and stay exempt.

The new check lives in c6_check_var_initialized() and is called from the
object-definition branch of decl(), after 'has_init' is known and before TCC
rewrites a tentative global definition into an 'extern' one.  The diagnostic
uses the identifier as written: a 'package' mangles the name only afterwards.

c6 test fixtures gain the missing initializers, and 165_c6_init
covers both directions plus the VLA / extern / parameter / member exemptions.

Tests: tests2 144/144 with C6_EXT, 165_c6_init uses -dt.
